 "semantics": "before overrides defaults; after overrides the complete before snapshot. Unlisted fields remain unchanged. Event adapters drive real handlers; Qt consumes corresponding STATE/ACK and resolves the listed pending request. No per-language expected-state copies. `reply` is normative: the exact packets the service emits for the event, in order; [] means none. ACK next_transaction/output_epoch/revision and every STATE field come from the `after` snapshot; STATE session_id is the case token unless `session_id` says `zero`. Python asserts emitted packets equal `reply`; Qt is fed exactly these packets. For INTERRUPT: fence <= N (the sender's one in-flight id); fence > N is ACK INVALID with no state change except last_control_id. A fenced id the service never saw (its BEGIN is delayed on the link) is retired as finish(id, kind 0, CANCELLED): last_kind 0 with last_transaction > 0 means that id never reached the service, and a client resolves its pending request with that id as Cancelled whatever its kind. qt.revision_seen is the last revision the client accepted and must be lower than the snapshot's revision whenever the snapshot's content differs from what the client saw (the service bumps the revision on every change).",
